687862230262,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.04001670382386946,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":56.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.16289169419233107,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0042504190797186606,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":15.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.00931904333307565,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":61.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.029892069736229755,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":50.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.04335,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":28.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Axos Financial, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides consumer and business banking products in the United States. It operates through two segments, Banking Business and Securities Business. The company offers various deposits products, including consumer and business checking, savings, and time deposits; and demand accounts, and money market accounts. It also provides residential single family, multifamily, and commercial mortgage loans; loans secured by commercial real estate properties; loans secured by commercial assets and non-bank lenders; auto and unsecured loans and other loans; and lender finance loans, asset-based loans, capital call facilities, equipment lending and leasing, retail and floor plan marine loans, and other consumer loans. In addition, the company offers a range of investment and wealth management services, such as disclosed clearing, recordkeeping, trade reporting, and reorganization assistance services, and securities clearing and custody, as well as margin loans and securities lending services; and retail self-directed and digital advice services. It offers it services through its digital online and mobile banking platforms, distribution channels, and affinity partners. The company was formerly known as BofI Holding, Inc. and changed its name to Axos Financial, Inc. in September 2018. Axos Financial, Inc. was incorporated in 1999 and is based in Las Vegas, Nevada.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Gregory  Garrabrants C.F.A., J.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $2.7M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $676K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 22%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $133K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $20K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Axos Financial, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $5.2B market cap on $1.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +18% over the past three years and +16% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 28% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 18-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $291M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.14\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.4%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.3% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.7\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 14% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 15% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 37% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Axos Financial (AX) Stock Still Trades At A Discount Following Its 137% Run","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-ax/axos-financial/news/axos-financial-ax-stock-still-trades-at-a-discount-following","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794382090.022,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.875,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(AX) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/40/AX_Movement_as_an_Input_in_Quant_Signal_Sets_111026124802_1794289682.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794289682.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Can Axos Financial (AX) Be A Bargain On Strong Quarterly Earnings?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-ax/axos-financial/news/can-axos-financial-ax-be-a-bargain-on-strong-quarterly-earni","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794248670.975,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.85,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Did Strong Quarterly Earnings Just Shift Axos Financial's (AX) Investment Narrative?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nyse-ax/axos-financial/news/did-strong-quarterly-earnings-just-shift-axos-financials-ax","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794158588.795,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.919,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Axos Financial (NYSE:AX) Dips Below A Key Level: Opportunity?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/financial/axos-financial-nyseax-dips-below-a-key-level-opportunity","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793973180.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.132,"tier":0,"sc